/-!
# The presentation of the Rudvalis group holds in its permutation model

The presentation selected for `Ru` (`TauCeti.Sporadic.ruPresentation`) is Soicher's presentation
on three generators `u`, `v` and `t`, of orders `4`, `2` and `2`, with twelve relators. The
generators `Ru.a` and `Ru.b` of the degree-4060 model `TauCeti.Sporadic.Ru` are the standard
generators of the ATLAS, so they are not such a family. This file gives three permutations
`Ru.imageU`, `Ru.imageV` and `Ru.imageT` of the `4060` points that satisfy all twelve relators and
generate exactly the model `Ru`, and deduces that the presented group `SporadicName.Ru.Group` maps
onto the model. In particular the presented group is nontrivial.

Each image is given by its table of images, so that the relators compute directly. Each is also
written as a word in the generators of the model (`Ru.imageU_eq`, `Ru.imageV_eq`,
`Ru.imageT_eq`), which puts it in the model; conversely `Ru.a_eq` and `Ru.b_eq` write the two
generators of the model as words in the three images, so the images generate the whole model.

The three permutations were found by computer. A coset enumeration of the presentation over the
subgroup generated by `t`, `u` and `((uvu)⁻¹tuvuvtv[t,u]²vtv)²`, the one the source of the
presentation names for that purpose, closes with `4060` cosets and gives the action of `u`, `v`
and `t` on them. That action and the model both preserve a graph of valency `1755` on the `4060`
points (an orbital of the rank-three action), and an isomorphism between the two graphs carries
the three coset permutations to the point numbering of the model; the result was then conjugated
inside the model so that `Ru.imageV` is the square of `Ru.b`. The words come from a search in the
Cayley graphs. Nothing about that computation is used: the relators and both directions of
generation are checked here. Products follow Mathlib's convention `(σ * τ) x = σ (τ x)`, and it is
in this convention that the relators are evaluated.

No order of the model or of the presented group is asserted here, and the surjection is not shown
to be injective.

The lift and range arguments use `GroupPresentation.homEquiv` and
`GroupPresentation.exists_surjective_of_closure_range_eq`.

## Main declarations

* `TauCeti.Sporadic.Ru.imageU`, `TauCeti.Sporadic.Ru.imageV`, `TauCeti.Sporadic.Ru.imageT`: the
  images of the three generators, with `TauCeti.Sporadic.Ru.presentationImage` the resulting
  assignment.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.Ru.lift_presentationImage_toFreeGroup_eq_one`: the twelve relators hold.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.Ru.imageU_mem`, `TauCeti.Sporadic.Ru.imageV_mem`,
  `TauCeti.Sporadic.Ru.imageT_mem`, `TauCeti.Sporadic.Ru.presentationImage_mem`: the images lie in
  the model.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.Ru.closure_range_presentationImage`: the images generate the model.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.Ru.presentationHom`, `TauCeti.Sporadic.Ru.range_presentationHom`,
  `TauCeti.Sporadic.Ru.presentationHom_mem`: the homomorphism from the presented group, its range,
  and the membership of its values in the model.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.exists_surjective_Ru`: the presented group maps onto the model.

## References

* L. H. Soicher, `tcenum`, presentation file `presentations/Ru`, commit
  `fb9dd89130fca8ad7dc4a92537c96ce7b30b62f1`,
  <https://github.com/lhsoicher/tcenum/blob/fb9dd89130fca8ad7dc4a92537c96ce7b30b62f1/presentations/Ru>,
  for the presentation and the subgroup of index `4060`.
* J. D. Bradley, R. T. Curtis, and M. Aslam Malik, *Symmetric generation of the Rudvalis group*,
  Journal of the London Mathematical Society **82** (2010), 643--662,
  <https://doi.org/10.1112/jlms/jdq039>.
* R. A. Wilson, R. A. Parker, J. N. Bray et al., *ATLAS of Finite Group Representations*,
  version 3, representation `RuG1-p4060B0`,
  <https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/v3/permrep/RuG1-p4060B0>, for the model in whose point
  numbering the images are given.
-/

